{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And he shall make the woman drink.</b> This is not the order of the procedure, for first he offers her meal-offering. Rather, Scripture informs you that when he makes her drink, they enter her to become bitter — for since belly and thigh are stated, whence for the rest of the body? Scripture says ״ובאו בה״ — in all of her. If so, what does Scripture mean by belly and thigh? Because they began the transgression first, therefore the punishment begins from them (Sifrei)." "<b>For bitterness.</b> To be harmful and bitter to her."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:33.918917389Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}